{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Bread and a skin of water.</b> And not silver and gold — because he hated him, on account of his having gone out into evil company." "<b>And the child.</b> The child too she placed on her shoulder, for Sarah had cast an evil eye upon him and a fever seized him and he could not walk on his feet (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>And she went and wandered.</b> She returned to the idols of her father's house (Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer, ch. 30)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:44.754393686Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}